-- title:
--   Centre pins for the chart-pinned generic fibre of the Igusa scheme
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $p$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid p$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) for the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` for the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $p$, and $L =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar p` for its base change along the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb` into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. Assume that $\bar{j} =$ `jBar p`, the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$, is transcendental over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and nonzero, and that $L$ is finite over each of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\bar{j})$ and $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\bar{j}^{-1})$. Assume given $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra isomorphisms $e_{\mathrm{fin}} \colon \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \mathrm{chartRing}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\{\bar{j}\}$ and $e_{\infty} \colon \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \mathcal{O}_{\infty} \to \mathrm{chartRing}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\{\bar{j}^{-1}\}$, where $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin p ℓ`, $\mathcal{O}_{\infty} =$ `chartAlgInf p ℓ`, and $\mathrm{chartRing}\,K\,S$ denotes the subalgebra of elements of $L$ integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $S$; it is assumed that $e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b)$ and $e_{\infty}(1 \otimes b)$ are, in both cases, the coefficientwise image in $L$ of the Laurent series $b \in F$. Let $M_\eta =$ `CurveModel.ofGenerator` be the two-chart curve model of $L$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ built from the generator $\bar{j}$. Then for every isomorphism $e_\eta$ from the underlying scheme of $M_\eta$ to the pullback of `igusaTo p ℓ` along $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection is the structure morphism of $M_\eta$, and which on the two charts is given by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $b \mapsto e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b)$ followed by `ιFin p ℓ`, respectively $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $b \mapsto e_{\infty}(1 \otimes b)$ followed by `ιInf p ℓ`, the following two assertions hold. For every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $x$ of $M_\eta$ (a section of the structure morphism) and every ring homomorphism $\gamma \colon \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $x$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\gamma$ followed by `ιFin p ℓ`, every $b \in \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$, viewed in $L$ via `coeffEmb`, lies in the valuation subring of the place $P(x) =$ `Mη.pointEquivPlace x` and satisfies $b - \gamma(b) \in$ the nonunits of that valuation subring; and the same statement with $\mathcal{O}_{\infty}$ and `ιInf p ℓ` in place of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and `ιFin p ℓ`.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre half of the centre-pin data used to compare points of the two-chart model of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(p))$ with points of the Igusa scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$: it says that a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point described on one of the two Igusa charts by a homomorphism $\gamma$ has, as its associated place, one whose valuation ring contains the chart algebra and whose maximal ideal contains $b - \gamma(b)$, so that $\gamma$ is the reduction map at that place. It feeds the lemmas of the Deligne–Rapoport model package that identify the reduction of a point and match the two chart-wise reduction maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_coeffEmb_sub_mem_nonunits_pointEquivPlace_ofGenerator_of_chartPin.lean

